      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not apply butter, lotion, or any ointment to a fresh burn, as these stick to the skin and can cause further damage while trapping bacteria. Instead, immediately run cool (not ice-cold) water over the affected area for at least 20 minutes to stop the burning process and soothe the pain. After cooling, gently cover the site with a sterile, non-stick bandage if possible to protect it from infection.",
